  "_comment": "Whether a remote path a user wrote or saved may be used as a location (joined to a root, stripped of a prefix, compared with a folder boundary). Read by the backend (src-tauri/src/util/path_location.rs, location_problem) and by the frontend (src/utils/syncNavigationPath.test.ts, locationProblem), so both refuse the same paths for the same reason. `/` and `\\` both end a step; a `.` step, a `..` step, an empty step (a doubled slash, except before a leading separator, the second one of a leading `\\\\` of a Windows UNC path, and after a single trailing separator) and a NUL are refused, never collapsed. A null problem means the path may be used. `savedProblem` is the reason a location ALREADY saved is refused (saved_location_problem / savedLocationProblem): only a `..` step and a NUL, which change where it points; its `.` and empty steps are left as saved.",
